      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Compact product navigation from website/style.css.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-web-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"#how-it-works\">How it works</a><a href=\"https://github.com/Tengify/promptbeacon\">Source</a><a class=\"ds-web-nav-download\" href=\"#downloads\">Get the app</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-web-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:34px;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:550;color:var(--ink,#18201e)}.ds-web-nav a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.ds-web-nav-download{border:1px solid var(--ink,#18201e);padding:9px 17px;border-radius:7px}.ds-web-nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:5px}.ds-web-nav a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#2870d5);outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:580px){.ds-web-nav{gap:15px;font-size:12px}.ds-web-nav>a:first-child{display:none}.ds-web-nav-download{padding:7px 10px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Website Appearance Switch",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Synthetic rehearsal control from website/style.css; state is demonstrated declaratively.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-web-switch\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Beacon appearance\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">Border</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Tint</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Badge</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-web-switch{display:inline-flex;gap:3px;background:#e4e8de;border-radius:7px;padding:3px}.ds-web-switch button{font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;font-size:12px;background:transparent;border:0;border-radius:5px;min-height:34px;padding:7px 13px;color:#4a564a;cursor:pointer}.ds-web-switch button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#fff;color:#1c271d;box-shadow:0 2px 5px #18201e18}.ds-web-switch button:hover{color:#172d1d}.ds-web-switch button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#2870d5);outline-offset:5px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Website Beacon Badge",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Synthetic model-and-effort signal from website/style.css.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-web-beacon\"><span class=\"ds-web-beacon-dot\"></span><div><strong>Model A</strong><span>High · Synthetic</span></div><span class=\"ds-web-bars\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"ds-web-filled\"></i><i class=\"ds-web-filled\"></i><i class=\"ds-web-filled\"></i><i></i><i></i></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-web-beacon{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;color:#fff;background:var(--ink,#18201e);border:1px solid var(--signal,#2870d5);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 13px;min-width:208px;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;transition:border-color .4s var(--ease,cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1))}.ds-web-beacon-dot{height:10px;width:10px;flex-shrink:0;background:var(--signal,#2870d5);border-radius:50%;transition:background .4s var(--ease,cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1))}.ds-web-beacon strong{display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}.ds-web-beacon div>span{display:block;color:#c4cdc7;font-size:10px}.ds-web-bars{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:3px;margin-left:9px;height:19px}.ds-web-bars i{width:3px;height:5px;background:#566359;border-radius:1px}.ds-web-bars i:nth-child(2){height:8px}.ds-web-bars i:nth-child(3){height:11px}.ds-web-bars i:nth-child(4){height:14px}.ds-web-bars i:nth-child(5){height:17px}.ds-web-bars i.ds-web-filled{background:var(--signal,#2870d5)}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-web-beacon,.ds-web-beacon-dot{transition:none}}",
      "refersTo": "website-beacon-badge"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Color-Calibration Bench",
    "overview": "PromptBeacon is a quiet instrument beside a coding session. Its established native interface stays in operate mode: neutral surfaces, precise swatches, a large window specimen, and compact live readouts. The active selection becomes a peripheral color signal with explicit effort notation. Reading and typing take priority over decoration.\n\nThe public website presents the same mechanism at a longer viewing distance. Warm paper, bold Sora headlines, and a dark geometric coding specimen explain the utility through an explicitly synthetic rehearsal. System typography continues to carry controls and practical detail. The website introduces the instrument; it does not replace the native utility's density, typography, or OS-responsive theme.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Color-calibration language: labeled swatches, window edges, and explicit effort bars.",
      "Native utility density alongside a spacious paper-based marketing surface.",
      "Self-hosted Sora for website display text; system typography for controls and native screens.",
      "Text equivalents and distinct state labels accompany every model signal.",
      "Synthetic, labeled demonstrations instead of private session captures."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Signal Integrity Rule",
        "body": "Model colors identify a selection. They never substitute for the model name, effort label, or unknown state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Working Distances Rule",
        "body": "Sora belongs to website display text. Native settings, website controls, and detailed explanations keep their established system faces.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Edge Rule",
        "body": "The real overlay remains a peripheral, non-interactive surface. Interactive rehearsal controls belong outside the overlay.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the native utility in operate mode, with Beacon, Model colors, and Connections as its settings sections.",
      "Do pair model color with a readable model name and pair effort bars with an explicit effort label.",
      "Do preserve visible distinctions between detected, preview, unknown, paused, waiting, permission-required, and error states.",
      "Do use the existing paper, system controls, and self-hosted Sora pairing for website additions.",
      "Do label illustrative sessions as synthetic and keep public examples independent of private settings, screenshots, and diagnostics.",
      "Do retain keyboard focus indicators and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn the native settings window into a marketing screen or a dashboard of invented metrics.",
      "Don't guess unavailable effort, present preview as live detection, or let a stale selection look current.",
      "Don't place interactive content in the real overlay or obscure the prompt with controls.",
      "Don't use display typography for native utility controls or scale synthetic specimen microcopy into general body typography.",
      "Don't introduce external font requests, private session captures, or local-machine paths into public design examples."
    ]
  }
}
